  "headline": "The effectiveness of implementing case-based learning in",
  "name": "The effectiveness of implementing case-based learning in",
  "description": "Objectives: This study aimed to identify and analyze\nin improving nursing students’ clinical skills, critical\nthinking, problem-solving, motivation, and satisfaction.\nMethods: A systematic review was employed. This\narticle has been compiled in accordance with the\nPRISMA method. Article searches were conducted\nusing PubMed, EBSCOhost, ProQuest, ScienceDirect,\nthe Cochrane Library, and Scopus. Structured research\nquestions using the PICO method, and search keywords\nbased on Boolean combinations. A total of 590 articles\nRecibido: 11 de diciembre 2025\nAceptado: 16 de enero 2026\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.47307/GMC.2026.134.1.17\nORCID: 0000-0002-6859-56751a\nORCID: 0009-0009-9765-29212\nORCID: 0000-0001-9111-211X3\nORCID: 0000-0002-2350-01504\nORCID: 0000-0002-2633-34825\nORCID: 0009-0003-8411-66676\nORCID: 0009-0002-7214-23347\nORCID: 0009-0005-4402-44478\n1aNursing Department, Sekolah Tinggi Ilmu Kesehatan Mayapada,\nJakarta, Indonesia\n2Department Maternity Nursing, Nursing Study Program, Sekolah\nTinggi Ilmu Kesehatan Maluku Husada, Indonesia\n3Department of Nursing, Universitas Tanjungpura, Indonesia\n4Department of Nursing, Faculty of Public Health, Universitas\nMuslim Indonesia\n5Department of Nursing, Universitas Sains Al-Qur’an, Indonesia\n6Department of Nursing, Akademi Keperawatan Kesdam Iskandar\nMuda Banda Aceh, Indonesia\n7,8Department of Nursing, Faculty of Nursing, Stikes Griya Husada,\nSumbawa, Indonesia\n1a Corresponding author: Muhammad Al-Amin R. Sapeni\nE-mail: muh.alamin@stikesmayapada.ac.id\nAddress: Semut Swamp Seclusion Street, Margahayu, Bekasi City,\nWest Java, Indonesia 17113\nPhone:+6282291875670 were identified, and 6 were included based on the\nresearch question. The included articles were assessed\nusing the Critical Appraisal Skills Programme and\nthe Mixed Methods Appraisal Tool. To determine the\narticle’ s quality, the Effective Public Health Practice\nProject was used. Results: There were 6 articles\nincluded in this study. Regarding the results of the\ncritical assessment, the implementation of case-based\nlearning can significantly improve nursing students’\nclinical skills, critical thinking, problem-solving,\nmotivation, and learning satisfaction. Conclusion:\nImplementing case-based learning for nursing students\ncan improve clinical skills, critical thinking, problem-\nsolving, motivation, and student satisfaction with\nlearning. Therefore, the CBL method is recommended\nfor nursing education.",
